{#-
  One paragraph of a mail body. Ported from view/sion-model/mailing/paragraph-partial.phtml.

  `type` is content (default), button or partial:
  - content: `content`, translated unless isTranslatorEnabled is false, escaped unless
    shouldEscape is false, then vsprintf'd with contentParams if isContentParameterized —
    see SionModel\Twig\MailExtension::content() for the order and its consequence;
  - button: the same text inside an anchor to `target` (printed verbatim, as before) with
    class buttonClass (default btn-primary). The old `urlArgs` alternative — assemble a
    laminas route — is gone: a mail has no request to build a URL from, so callers pass
    the absolute `target`;
  - partial: includes the template named by `partial` with this paragraph's variables.
-#}
{%- set type = type is defined and type in ['content', 'partial', 'button'] ? type : 'content' -%}
{%- if type == 'partial' -%}
    {%- if partial is defined %}{{ include(partial) }}{% endif -%}
{%- elseif type == 'button' -%}
<a href="{{ target is defined and target is not null ? target|raw : '' }}" class="{{ (buttonClass is defined and buttonClass is not null ? buttonClass : 'btn-primary')|e('html_attr') }}" itemprop="url">{{ mail_content(_context) }}</a>
    {% else -%}
{{ mail_content(_context) }}
{%- endif -%}
